order to subtract the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. Here, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of $z(w-1)$ if we multiply the top and bottom of the second fraction by $-z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{z(w-1)}-\\frac{1}{1-w} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{z(w-1)}-\\frac{(-z)}{(-z)}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-w} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{z(w-1)}+\\frac{z}{z(w-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{z+3}{z(w-1)} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533717 true] [17592186248198 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248199 13194139533717 true] [17592186248198 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248200 13194139533717 true] [17592186248198 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248201 13194139533717 true] [17592186248198 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248202 13194139533717 true] [17592186248198 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248203 13194139533717 true] [17592186248198 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533717 true] [17592186248198 1041 "selection" 13194139533717 true] [17592186248198 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248203 13194139533717 true] [17592186248198 1110 #uuid "e28c27a7-325c-5eba-9980-2849411f29d7" 13194139533717 true] [17592186248199 1034 "\\frac{-z+2}{z(w-1)}" 13194139533717 true] [17592186248199 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533717 true] [17592186248199 1111 #uuid "c6a0a30e-3f82-5798-9030-365e590ddd5b" 13194139533717 true] [17592186248200 1034 "\\frac{2w}{z(w-1)}" 13194139533717 true] [17592186248200 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533717 true] [17592186248200 1111 #uuid "cb0feeb3-911c-5013-9d5b-3155a62dbdbf" 13194139533717 true] [17592186248201 1034 "\\frac{w+3}{z(w-1)}" 13194139533717 true] [17592186248201 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533717 true] [17592186248201 1111 #uuid "360d371b-f170-5783-acb5-c3af763a767c" 13194139533717 true] [17592186248202 1034 "\\frac{z-6}{z(w-1)}" 13194139533717 true] [17592186248202 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533717 true] [17592186248202 1111 #uuid "365725af-9bb0-5094-9de5-ec9d0767803e" 13194139533717 true] [17592186248203 1034 "\\frac{z+3}{z(w-1)}" 13194139533717 true] [17592186